title RecruitBook Batch 5 — Effective Admissions Visibility Decision

' ============================================================
' NOT a state machine — no named ProfileVisibilitySettings states,
' no lifecycle transitions, no state-model number. This is the
' single is_admissions_visible_profile(profile_id) decision,
' re-evaluated at query time by BOTH discovery and direct view.
' ============================================================

start
:Caller requests profile_id\n(via discovery list OR\ndirect /admissions/students/[id]);

if (Access precondition:\nis_verified_admissions_officer()?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:NOT VISIBLE\n(role gate fails — pending/\nsuspended/unverified officer);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (1. Does a profile_visibility_settings\nrow exist for this profile_id?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:NOT VISIBLE\n(missing row is NOT\nimplicitly visible);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (2. is_published = true?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:NOT VISIBLE;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (3. admissions_consent = true?) then (no)
  #FEE2E2:NOT VISIBLE;
  stop
else (yes)
  #DCFCE7:4. EFFECTIVELY VISIBLE\nto this verified admissions officer;
  stop
endif

note right
  This decision IS
  is_admissions_visible_profile(profile_id).
  Evaluated AT QUERY TIME on every call —
  no derived or cached visibility field
  exists anywhere. Flipping either
  is_published or admissions_consent to
  false immediately returns the profile
  to NOT VISIBLE on the very next check.
end note

note right
  The SAME decision gates BOTH the
  discovery list (Flow B) and the direct
  detail route — there is no separate
  "list visibility" vs "detail visibility."
end note

note as N_RoleGate
  is_verified_admissions_officer() is an
  ACCESS PRECONDITION on the CALLER, not a
  state of the profile's own lifecycle.
  It does not change with is_published or
  admissions_consent, and it is re-checked
  independently on every request.
end note

note as N_NotALifecycle
  Deliberately NOT modeled here (no SM
  number assigned; not a state machine):
  * Named ProfileVisibilitySettings states/
    transitions (e.g. NotPublished,
    PublishedVisible, PublishedHidden) —
    the long-term SM-6 model in the master
    catalogs remains unbuilt.
  * A separate ConsentSettings table.
  * Whether an already-visible SUSPENDED
    student's profile stays visible — an
    OPEN Group 2 design question, not
    decided by this diagram either way.
end note

@enduml
